{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And they looked out toward the face of Sedom.</b> Rashi's comment: every השקפה in Scripture is for evil, except 'the looking out from Your holy habitation' etc. One may object: but it is written 'Who is this that looks forth' (מי זאת הנשקפה), and 'until he looks out and sees' (עד ישקיף וירא), and 'righteousness from the heavens looks forth' (צדק משמים נשקף), and 'for he looked out from his holy habitation' (כי השקיף ממעון קדשו)." "<b>He walked with them to send them off.</b> Rashi's comment: an expression of escorting, for he thought they were travelers, and even when it was said to him 'I will return to you,' he thought he was a prophet speaking in the name of HaShem."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The comment cites Rashi by name and then voices an objection with חז״ק, which appears to be an abbreviated form of 'one may object' (יש לומר / קושיא); rendered accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:45.073861303Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}